(1778989, 239532, 35357, '<td valign="top">Hehe, curse of the Woodies. ;-)</td>', 'Hehe, curse of the Woodies. ;-)', '2005-10-12 09:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1778992, 239996, 25728, '<td valign="top">Oh it was so nice to see a photojournalistic style photo get a ribbon. Congrats! It is well deserved.</td>', 'Oh it was so nice to see a photojournalistic style photo get a ribbon. Congrats! It is well deserved.', '2005-10-12 09:02:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1778996, 237485, 41381, '<td valign="top"><b>After the result :</b> <br/> <br/>I think the fact that I do not have photoshop, costed me a place in the top ten ! For that is why, I could not put unsharp mask and the pic looks really distorted after compressing the pixel size. Also after the sepia tone was done in Picasa, the pic lost its sharpness, donno why. Sadyly, the original was razor sharp.<br/>So the good software costed me my very first top ten finish, and I rue the fact !<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-12 08:07:49.</i></td>', 'After the result :  I think the fact that I do not have photoshop, costed me a place in the top ten ! For that is why, I could not put unsharp mask and the pic looks really distorted after compressing the pixel size. Also after the sepia tone was done in Picasa, the pic lost its sharpness, donno why. Sadyly, the original was razor sharp.So the good software costed me my very first top ten finish, and I rue the fact !', '2005-10-12 09:05:15.000000', '2005-10-12 09:07:49.000000', 0),
(1779004, 239049, 32767, '<td valign="top">Nice image. You captured a great coffe shop vibe.</td>', 'Nice image. You captured a great coffe shop vibe.', '2005-10-12 09:10:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779005, 240595, 29154, '<td valign="top">Hi JD,<br/> <br/>I hope you won''t get me wrong with this comment, but I saw your color version on PBase and never understood why you summitted a BW .... The color one is just STUNNING !!  20th position is very good, but I think you would have finished higher with the color one.  Cheers</td>', 'Hi JD, I hope you won''t get me wrong with this comment, but I saw your color version on PBase and never understood why you summitted a BW .... The color one is just STUNNING !!  20th position is very good, but I think you would have finished higher with the color one.  Cheers', '2005-10-12 09:11:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779019, 240509, 34956, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju með top 20.</td>', 'Til hamingju með top 20.', '2005-10-12 09:20:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779041, 239049, 26633, '<td valign="top">Sorry I didn''t have time to comment during the challenge itself. Nice work.<br/> <br/>I gave you a 7 for this one. It would have been one of my favourites in the challenge but it had two "faults" (personal opinion only) which bothered me. One is that the subject of the picture is a bit too soft for my liking, my preference would be to see him a little sharper. The other is that I don''t see any benefit in tilting the camera. I always knock a point off for that ;)<br/> <br/>The burnt out window, crockery and table top just add to the atmosphere. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Sorry I didn''t have time to comment during the challenge itself. Nice work. I gave you a 7 for this one. It would have been one of my favourites in the challenge but it had two "faults" (personal opinion only) which bothered me. One is that the subject of the picture is a bit too soft for my liking, my preference would be to see him a little sharper. The other is that I don''t see any benefit in tilting the camera. I always knock a point off for that ;) The burnt out window, crockery and table top just add to the atmosphere.  ', '2005-10-12 09:33:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779068, 240427, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved blue with this clever Coffee Shop shot! Would be cool to see the whole set-up... where the "face" was positioned in relation to the lightning etc... and maybe the underware part too! Glad to see your efforts paid off in capturing the Blue!</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved blue with this clever Coffee Shop shot! Would be cool to see the whole set-up... where the "face" was positioned in relation to the lightning etc... and maybe the underware part too! Glad to see your efforts paid off in capturing the Blue!', '2005-10-12 09:50:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779076, 239996, 42574, '<td valign="top">A very nice, friendly, cozy feel comming across here. Congratulations!</td>', 'A very nice, friendly, cozy feel comming across here. Congratulations!', '2005-10-12 09:55:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779086, 240427, 24951, '<td valign="top">Yes, I agree  - this is well deserved. What a great idea well executed. Much success.</td>', 'Yes, I agree  - this is well deserved. What a great idea well executed. Much success.', '2005-10-12 10:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779091, 240070, 42574, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!</td>', 'Congratulations!', '2005-10-12 10:03:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779092, 239532, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very good idea!  Sharp wit and focus.<br/> <br/>I think overall this is a very good image.  I think you were penalized for having a woody ;)<br/> <br/>Compositionally, however, I think this could have been a little stronger.      I''m not fixated on the rule of thirds, but this image could be balanced better by using it.  My first thought is that the paper goods on the left weren''t needed and don''t provide compositional balance, and you could have thus cropped on that side and tried to get woody in the sweet spot--right now he and the coffee maker are too close to center.  <br/> <br/>Second, I think the brown/dark background makes the beans on the left less effective.  If I were to imagine arranging the scene, I might have done the following (but realize this is not easy to previsualize so I may be totally off base): ditch the paper cups on the right, put the beans there in a more prominent position, shifting the maker left, and balancing the maker on the left with the beans on the right.  Put in a very nice expresso cup, either filled with steaming coffee or money.  The latter idea has me thinking a little bit: to make a statement about coffee costs, the jar isn''t really "unambiguous" because it is associated with tips, not the cost of coffee.  So maybe the coffee cup idea filled with money, or some foreground with money and coffee somehow intermingled in either a natural or artistic statement way.<br/> <br/>Alternate title: Hey buddy, can I have $5 for a cup of coffee? ;)</td>', 'Very good idea!  Sharp wit and focus. I think overall this is a very good image.  I think you were penalized for having a woody ;) Compositionally, however, I think this could have been a little stronger.      I''m not fixated on the rule of thirds, but this image could be balanced better by using it.  My first thought is that the paper goods on the left weren''t needed and don''t provide compositional balance, and you could have thus cropped on that side and tried to get woody in the sweet spot--right now he and the coffee maker are too close to center.   Second, I think the brown/dark background makes the beans on the left less effective.  If I were to imagine arranging the scene, I might have done the following (but realize this is not easy to previsualize so I may be totally off base): ditch the paper cups on the right, put the beans there in a more prominent position, shifting the maker left, and balancing the maker on the left with the beans on the right.  Put in a very nice expresso cup, either filled with steaming coffee or money.  The latter idea has me thinking a little bit: to make a statement about coffee costs, the jar isn''t really "unambiguous" because it is associated with tips, not the cost of coffee.  So maybe the coffee cup idea filled with money, or some foreground with money and coffee somehow intermingled in either a natural or artistic statement way. Alternate title: Hey buddy, can I have $5 for a cup of coffee? ;)', '2005-10-12 10:03:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779094, 240070, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first Ribbon with a glowing rendition of this caffiene machine! I have one of these in my shop (very expensive, whats it doing in your mom''s patio?) but my work and my imagination didn''t seem to come together. Great work, I''m sure this will be the first of many more to come!</td>', 'Congratulations on your first Ribbon with a glowing rendition of this caffiene machine! I have one of these in my shop (very expensive, whats it doing in your mom''s patio?) but my work and my imagination didn''t seem to come together. Great work, I''m sure this will be the first of many more to come!', '2005-10-12 10:04:04.000000', NULL, 0),
